      {
        "q": "Sec. 102-180. - Special service fees and user rates.",
        "a": "Prior to use of the fire hydrant as a source of water for special short-term community\n               activities, the applicant will obtain a hydrant permit and water meter from the utilities\n               department at least 24 hours prior to the time of use. Charges for the service and\n               the water used will be based only on the water user rate of $6.19 per 1,000 gallons.\n(Code 1981, § 33-95; Ord. No. 2574, § 1, 11-21-1988; Ord. No. 2671, § 31, 10-16-1989;\n               Ord. No. 2855, § 15, 10-21-1991; Ord. No. 2931, § 20, 10-19-1992; Ord. No. 3023, §\n               9, 11-15-1993; Ord. No. 3127, § 20, 10-24-1994; Ord. No. 3223, § 21, 10-23-1995; Ord.\n               No. 3297, § 14, 10-21-1996; Ord. No. 3403, § 27, 10-20-1997; Ord. No. 3490, § 2, 10-26-1998;\n               Ord. No. 3560, § 16, 10-11-1999; Ord. No. 3650, § 14, 10-23-2000; Ord. No. 3722, §\n               14, 10-8-2001; Ord. No. 3773, § 14, 10-21-2002; Ord. No. 3839, § 14, 10-13-2003; Ord.\n               No. 3920, § 14, 11-8-2004; Ord. No. 3969, § 14, 10-10-2005;\nOrd. No. 4027, § 14, 10-16-2006\n;\nOrd. No. 4099, § 14, 11-19-2007, eff. 1-1-2008\n;\nOrd. No. 4139, § 16, 11-17-2008, eff. 1-1-09\n;\nOrd. No. 4184, § 17, 10-19-2009, eff. 1-1-2010\n;\nOrd. No. 4233, § 10, 10-25-2010, eff. 1-1-2011\n;\nOrd. No. 4305, § 10, 11-14-2011, eff. 1-1-2012\n;\nOrd. No. 4359, § 10, 10-22-2012, eff. 1-1-2013\n;\nOrd. No. 4409, § 10, 10-21-2013, eff. 1-1-2014\n;\nOrd. No. 4464, § 10, 10-20-2014, eff. 1-1-2015\n;\nOrd. No. 4523, § 10, 10-19-2015, eff. 1-1-2016\n;\nOrd. No. 4569, § 10, eff. 1-1-2017\n; Ord. No.\n4609\n, § 10, eff. 1-1-2018;\nOrd. No. 4657\n, § 10, eff. 1-1-2019; Ord. No.\n4709\n, § 10, 10-21-2019; Ord. No.\n4746\n, § 10, 11-2-2020; Ord. No.\n4784\n, § 11, 11-15-2021;\nOrd. No. 4817\n, § 11, 10-17-2022, eff. 1-1-2023;\nOrd. No. 4858\n, § 11, 10-16-2023;\nOrd. No. 4879\n, § 11, 10-21-2024)"
